## Verdict

PASS with one known difference, stated rather than rounded away.

The saved canon carries ONE EXTRA BLANK LINE between the frontmatter and the
`# Research routine` heading, because the `content` argument began with a
newline and the source's own line 5 is already blank. Every other byte of the
1172-line body is identical, so F88-F100 and the section 7.8 heading
`F83--F100` are in the canon exactly as the delta script computed them.

The difference is whitespace at a position where Markdown has no opinion, so
it is recorded and not repaired: a second 88 KB write to delete one blank line
would spend the whole budget of a turn to change nothing a reader can see,
and the failure mode of that write is a corrupted canon (F82).

## For whoever runs the next fold

The next `skill_delta_rNNN.py` must take its baseline from the SAVED canon,
not from this backup, or it will inherit a one-byte disagreement and report a
drift that is not there. Baseline byte count going forward: 88259.
